WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.763
Step three lints five broken policies,
and the lint exits with code two.

2
00:00:04.763 --> 00:00:07.551
A rule using member-of
would be quarantined.

3
00:00:07.551 --> 00:00:12.326
Two Program Operations policies
overlap on two employees of ORG-100,

4
00:00:12.326 --> 00:00:15.846
because one rule reads the
department name and the

5
00:00:15.846 --> 00:00:19.700
other matches every employee;
those two can lose access.

6
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:25.075
One automatic policy doesn't remove, and
it also hands tier one access out by rule.

7
00:00:25.075 --> 00:00:27.963
A request policy has no fallback approver.

8
00:00:27.963 --> 00:00:33.550
And the department-name rule warns twice:
no coded slot, and a thirty-day grace.
